{"type":"assistant","uuid":"792925bc-f00e-491e-9fbe-25ffc2957082","session_id":"15ac22d5-ebe7-4127-864a-afafa01a191e","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"792925bc-f00e-491e-9fbe-25ffc2957082","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nHere's a summary of the fix:\n\n## Bug Analysis\n\n**Root Cause:** When entering an invalid Base32 secret (like \"test\") in the \"Enter details\" dialog, the `Entry` constructor directly calls `Base32.decode()` which throws an `IllegalArgumentException` when the input is not valid Base32. This unhandled exception crashes the app.\n\n**Stack trace location:** `Entry.java:90` → `ManualEntryDialog.java:210`\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**Two files modified:**\n\n### 1. `Entry.java` — Add defensive Base32 decoding\n\nAdded a private helper method `decodeSecret(String)` that wraps the Base32 decoding in a try-catch. If the input is invalid Base32, it throws a `RuntimeException` with a descriptive message instead of letting the raw `IllegalArgumentException` propagate.\n\nChanged all 4 places where `Base32().decode()` was called to use the new helper instead.\n\n### 2. `ManualEntryDialog.java` — Catch the exception and show error\n\nWrapped the Entry creation code in the \"Save\" button handler with a try-catch that catches `RuntimeException`. On error:\n- Sets an inline error on the secret field (`secretInput.setError()`)\n- Shows a `Toast` message with the error\n\n## Patch File\n\nThe patch is saved at: `fix-invalid-secret-crash.patch`\n\n## Build Note\n\nThe project could not be built in this environment due to network restrictions preventing Gradle from downloading the Android Gradle Plugin 3.5.3. The code changes are syntactically correct Java/Android code that follows the project's existing patterns (similar error handling is used in `ScanQRCodeFromFile.java`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":67542,"output_tokens":373,"cache_read_input_tokens":67072,"total_tokens":67915}}}
